# Layer-first

Top folders are the layers. The feature name repeats inside each one. The composition root is the only file that sees every concrete type.

## Serverpod

```
lib/src/domain/notes/
lib/src/application/notes/
lib/src/infra/notes/
lib/src/presentation/notes/
lib/src/presentation/mappers/wire_mappers.dart
lib/src/app/
```

Wire mappers for every feature live in `presentation/mappers/`. A new feature adds `domain/<name>/`, `application/<name>/`, `infra/<name>/`, and `presentation/<name>/`. It does not add a new top-level folder.

## Flutter

```
lib/domain/notes/
lib/application/notes/
lib/data/notes/
lib/presentation/notes/     page, notifier, and tile
lib/presentation/router/
lib/app/providers.dart
```

There is no `ui/` folder and no `presentation/features/`. The tile sits beside the page and does not import Riverpod.

## Rules

- A use case lives in `application/<feature>/`, never under `presentation/`.
- A second feature repeats its name in every layer. Shared failures live in `domain/shared/`.
- Tests mirror the layers: `test/unit/domain/`, `test/unit/application/`, then one test that crosses the outer edge.
